Z||000000||Neal||09-27-2001||01:32 AM||||doing a bit of rust repair in the rear wheel wells and im running int two obstacles<P>i need to remove the trunk fan and the fuel canister that is in the passange side wheel well.<P>For the trunk fan, i must be missing somthing because i took off the two nuts on top of the housing and i looks like it should pull off, but it doesnt.  What am i missing?<P>And for the fuel canister there are 3 main screws holding it in (triangle shaped) but the upper one close to the front is impossible to get at.  Is there any way to get at this without removing body panels?||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||09-27-2001||11:11 AM||||I think there are a couple of nuts under the fan as well.  If you have rust in this area, I'll bet it's on the outer side of the wheel well/trunk as well.  If you remove the inner plastic wheel well and perhaps the quarter panel, it's quite easy to get into this area.<BR>Gary||||reg||11
Z||000002||Fie Ro||09-27-2001||04:01 PM||||I can recall I had the same question (quite a long time ago) while I was disassembling my crashed GT, I think there's one more screw hidden "on the dark side of the fan!". Just have a good look where it can be! Or it's some kind of "click" system that keeps the fan in place (sorry I can't really recall that) The corner where the fan sits CAN be rusty but that isn't the reason it won't come loose......good luck<P>------------------<BR>-The Beauty & The Beast-<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero GT & <BR>1977 Dodge W200||||reg||1
